# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
config/api_keys.json          # your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/certs/                 # the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/whatsapp_web/          # a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands
                              # somebody your WhatsApp account, not just a key
**/token*.json                # Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/client_secret*.json        # Google OAuth client secrets
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
# memory/long_term.json  <-- Committing this publishes personal facts you told me
#memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
# The throwaway environment `pyinstaller` is run from, its console output, and
# the spec file it regenerates on every build — a second, staler copy of the
# command in .github/workflows/build-installers.yml, which is the source of
# truth.
#
# These are on their own lines on purpose: a trailing `# comment` in .gitignore
# is not a comment, it is part of the pattern, and the pattern then never
# matches. Several entries above are written that way too — the duplicated
# bare `config/api_keys.json` further down is what actually protects that file.
.venv-build/
.build-log/
JARVIS.spec

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
config/api_keys.json
config/api_keys.json
config/certs/jarvis.key
config/api_keys.json
